<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair to cut 36 jobs in France.</title>
<headline>Swissair to cut 36 jobs in France.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swissair AG said it was planning to cut 36 of 217 jobs in France and reduce salaries from January 1, 1997 as part of its overall plan to improve group profits by 500 million Swiss francs by 1998.</p>
<p>Swissair said in a statement that it would cut 66 jobs, but create 30 new jobs while around 15 jobs would be created through outsourcing.</p>
<p>The plan has been presented to French unions.</p>
<p>The restructuring includes the partial outsourcing of Swissair's cargo activities to an external handling agent at the Charles-de-Gaulle airport near Paris. This is planned to take effect on January 1.</p>
<p>Swissair also plans to restructure passenger operations in France with these measures to take effect on March 1, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
